      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "My date must be correct that this restaurant's menu is only meat or meatless. Because if there was a dish with no meat and pasta, it would not be meatless with pasta!\nSo out of the four meatless dishes, two can be eaten. Or $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}$ of all of the items on the menu can be eaten.\n2) There are 10 - 4 = 6 non-meat dishes.\n3) Divide that by 6. 1/2.\n4) Crossed out 1/4 because they made meatless but had pasta.\n5) 6- 3 = 3 non-meat pasta.\n6) Divide that by 6.1/2.\n7) 1/2 + 1/2 = 1.\n8) 10 - 4 = 6 total items.\n9) .75 or 3/4 is what I can eat.\n\n\n \n\n\nhttp://i.imgur.com/sXEr0hh.png[/img]\nMy other option would be to combine the first two equations, then combining the two sub-quests down the equation. No problem on the first. The second I came across a trick of simplifying things. $4/10$ becomes $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5]}$ and $3$ becomes $3/10$. I mixed it up a bit, but my main focus was on what I could eat. I can get three out of four meatless, then I can get three out of six meatless and pasta.",
